From 301d1c04b9dfe67d4cbc00e27bba852b3ee67fb3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sun, 11 Oct 2026 23:28:07 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Audit fix a: contract catalog follows option decisions,
 league moves and the ledger

The contract catalog (runtime/player_contracts.py, read only by the contract
pages and Wade's Contract tab; no decision path reads it) now:
- lays every applied League/option_decisions.json decision over the agreement
  whose option it decides, honouring the sheet's team_option_season and
  fourth_year_option_deadline (Wade's 2006-07 option: exercised 2005-10-31 at
  $3,201,202); a declined option, opt-out or exercised early termination ends
  the agreement with the season before it;
- adds the league contract ledger's carried contracts that no dated record
  shows (the 2003 first-round scale contracts), and ends an open salary
  fragment that the next ledger does not carry;
- applies every holder change in date order to the agreement in force: summer
  and Miami trades, the expansion draft, real trades and waivers before the
  symmetric league, and the dated league moves (trade and claim assign,
  ten_day and rest_of_season are new agreements, waive, clear, expire and
  retire close on their date); an agreement's club is its latest assignment's
  and a renamed club shows its current name;
- ends Miami sheet and archive agreements at their last scheduled season;
- treats an unrecorded amount as unknown when matching records (P.J. Brown is
  one agreement at $8.5M);
- names a register "signs with" club only for a player without a dated club;
- derives the displayed status from the agreement in force on the cutoff.
The page refresh removes contract pages whose id left the catalog, and the
freshness check reports one left on disk.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01ExmaEeFA7X8K2pJG6n4PLH
